---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Written against the GDPR, the German Federal Data Protection Act (BDSG) and
 * the Telecommunications Digital Services Data Protection Act (TDDDG), with a
 * short section for visitors elsewhere. Every data flow below is read from
 * the code; if one changes, this page changes in the same commit:
 *
 *   hosting        GitHub Pages serves every file (public/CNAME, deploy.yml);
 *                  the domain's DNS is at Cloudflare, requests go to GitHub.
 *   live counts    LiveCount.tsx and StarGlobe.tsx call api.github.com and
 *                  discord.com from the browser on load, and cache the numbers
 *                  in sessionStorage.
 *   videos         BuiltInPublic.astro creates the youtube-nocookie.com iframe
 *                  only when the visitor presses play; posters are local.
 *   nothing else   no cookies, no analytics, no web fonts from a CDN, no forms.
 *
 * The app section describes the desktop app's Google connections, read from
 * the app repo: jarvis/marketplace/auth/oauth_pkce_loopback.py (sign-in on
 * Google's page, tokens), jarvis/marketplace/token_store.py (OS credential
 * store), jarvis/marketplace/revoke.py (disconnect) and the native Google
 * tools under jarvis/plugins/tool/ (direct calls to Google's APIs).
 */
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";
import { IMPRINT_HREF, OPERATOR } from "@/lib/legal";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy — Personal Jarvis"
  description="What personaljarvis.ai does with personal data: no cookies, no analytics, and exactly which services your browser talks to."
  heading="Privacy policy"
>
  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and runs <strong>no analytics or tracking</strong>.</li>
    <li>There are no accounts, no forms and no newsletter.</li>
    <li>
      Your browser talks to three other services: GitHub (which hosts the site
      and supplies the star count), Discord (member count) and — only if you
      press play on a video — YouTube.
    </li>
    <li>We never receive a record of your visit ourselves.</li>
    <li>
      The Personal Jarvis app keeps Google data you connect on your own
      computer; we never receive it. See
      <a href="#app-google-data">the app and your Google data</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:</p>
  <address>
    {OPERATOR.name}<br />
    {OPERATOR.street}<br />
    {OPERATOR.city}<br />
    {OPERATOR.country}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>
  </address>
  <p>
    See also the <a href={IMPRINT_HREF}>imprint</a>. We are not required to
    appoint a data protection officer.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P.
    Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. To deliver the pages,
    GitHub processes your IP address, the date and time of the request, the
    page requested, the referring page and your browser's user agent, and may
    keep this in server logs for security purposes. We have no access to these
    logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR: our legitimate interest in
    delivering the site securely and reliably. GitHub is certified under the
    EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework, so transfers to the USA rely on the
    European Commission's adequacy decision (Article 45 GDPR). Details:
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The domain's DNS is provided by Cloudflare, Inc. Your requests for this
    site are not routed through Cloudflare.
  </p>

  <h2>Live counts from GitHub and Discord</h2>
  <p>
    Some numbers on this page are fetched live when the page loads: the
    project's star count from GitHub's public API (api.github.com) and the
    member count of our Discord server from Discord's public API
    (discord.com). For this, your browser connects directly to these services,
    which receive your IP address and browser information. No login and no
    cookie is involved, and we do not receive any of this data.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR: our legitimate interest in
    showing current figures instead of outdated ones. Both providers are based
    in the USA (GitHub, Inc.; Discord Inc., 444 De Haro Street, San Francisco,
    CA 94107) and are certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework. See
    <a href="https://discord.com/privacy">Discord's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    So that the numbers are not fetched again on every page view, your browser
    keeps them in its session storage until you close the tab. This stores
    only the public numbers, no personal data, and is strictly necessary for
    the function you see (Section 25(2) No. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>

  <h2>Videos</h2>
  <p>
    The video section shows a still image stored on this site. Nothing is
    loaded from YouTube until you press play. When you do, the video is
    embedded from youtube-nocookie.com, operated by Google Ireland Limited,
    Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. Google then receives your
    IP address and device information and may store information on your
    device, including for playback statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pressing play is your consent to this (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR, Section 25(1)
    TDDDG). Data may be transferred to Google LLC in the USA, which is
    certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework. You can withdraw your
    consent at any time with effect for the future by not playing videos and
    clearing your browser data. Details:
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Downloads and the source code are on GitHub; the site also links to X,
    Discord and YouTube. Once you follow such a link, the privacy policy of
    that provider applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="app-google-data">The Personal Jarvis app and your Google data</h2>
  <p>
    The Personal Jarvis desktop app can connect to your Google account —
    Gmail, Google Drive, Google Calendar, YouTube and Google Cloud — only when
    you click Connect in the app and approve access on Google's own sign-in
    page. Each service is connected separately.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What the app accesses.</strong> Only the Google services you
    connect, and only to carry out what you ask Jarvis to do — for example
    reading your calendar to answer "what is on today", or adding a song to a
    YouTube playlist you named.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Where the data goes.</strong> The app runs on your own computer.
    It fetches Google data directly from Google's APIs, and it stores the
    access and refresh tokens in your operating system's credential store on
    that computer. We, the developer, never receive, store or see your Google
    data or tokens. When you ask Jarvis about your data, the relevant excerpt
    is sent to the AI model provider you chose in the app, solely to answer
    that request; that provider's own privacy policy applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What we never do.</strong> We do not sell Google user data, use it
    for advertising, transfer it to data brokers, or use it to train or
    improve generalized artificial intelligence or machine-learning models.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Limited Use.</strong> Personal Jarvis' use and transfer of
    information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Revoking access.</strong> Disconnect the service in the app, or
    remove Personal Jarvis at
    <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">myaccount.google.com/connections</a>.
    Disconnecting deletes the stored tokens from your computer.
  </p>

  <h2>Contacting us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we use your address and message only to reply (Article
    6(1)(f) GDPR, or Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where your message concerns a
    contract). We delete the correspondence once it is no longer needed,
    unless we are legally required to keep it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Mail to our contact address is received by Cloudflare Email Routing
    (Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA) and
    forwarded to a mailbox hosted by Google (Google Ireland Limited). Both
    process the message only to deliver it. Cloudflare and Google LLC are
    certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Article 15),</li>
    <li>have it corrected (Article 16) or erased (Article 17),</li>
    <li>restrict its processing (Article 18),</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format (Article 20),</li>
    <li>
      <strong>object</strong> at any time to processing based on Article
      6(1)(f), on grounds relating to your particular situation (Article 21),
    </li>
    <li>withdraw a consent at any time with effect for the future (Article 7(3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, email
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>. You also have
    the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority, in particular in the EU member state where you live or work or
    where the alleged infringement took place (Article 77 GDPR). The
    authority responsible for us is the Bavarian State Office for Data
    Protection Supervision (Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht),
    Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach, Germany.
  </p>
  <p>
    Providing personal data is neither a legal nor a contractual requirement.
    We do not use automated decision-making or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Visitors outside the EU</h2>
  <p>
    We apply the standards above to every visitor, wherever you are. If you
    are in the United Kingdom, you have the same rights under the UK GDPR and
    may complain to the Information Commissioner's Office. If you are in
    California: we do not sell or share personal information, and we do not
    use it for targeted advertising. Anyone can exercise the rights described
    above by email.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p class="legal-doc__note">
    We update this policy when the site changes how it handles data. The date
    at the top shows the current version.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
